            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to scratch, then the German for to put cream on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: verstauchen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "verstauchen — \"to sprain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Beim Fußball habe ich mir den Fuß verstaucht. I sprained my foot playing football."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a dative of the person: sich den Fuß verstauchen. Inseparable: hat verstaucht."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "verstauchen is built on ver- and stauchen \"to compress, to jolt\" (EtymDB): a joint pushed out of shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
